ow i  am a complete wuss when it comes to this  sort of thing  so if you're a bit hesitant to go into  this sort of procedural route  then one of the few things that you can  do at home that will actually help is  microcurrent so this  is the ferro bear it is an at-home  microcurrent device  i did a video on how microcurrent works  and how to use the furrowed bear  so check that out if you want more  details microcurrent can make your face  look more lifted  it changes how your muscles tense up and  it can give you the appearance of more  volume  it doesn't seem to have much effect on  fat and bone but it does seem to  increase your muscle volume and  volume is volume you can generally see  the effects pretty immediately so the  most obvious ones are usually in your  cheeks they become more lifted and more  sculpted  and in your forehead as well in general  the effect is going to be more dramatic  if your face is starting to droop a bit  so if you're in your late teens or early  20s then  the effect you're going to see is  probably going to be very limited  but from your mid to late 20s onwards  then you can start to really see that  effect  after just using it once you use it for  only two to three minutes a day  and the effect lasts for a few days so  you do have to keep on using it to  maintain the look  and the more you use it the more that  effect builds up i've seen some people  say that because it's a temporary effect  it's not worth it and i disagree  i think that perspective that something  temporary something that lasts a few  days  isn't worth it comes mostly from people  who don't wear makeup  i think people who use makeup regularly  know that things that are more subtle  things that are temporary can have a big  effect on your appearance  and microcurrent is less temporary than  makeup  and it can have a more dramatic effect  that you can't really get easily with  makeup unless you are super talented  and of course because it goes deeper  than skin care