nly really deal with very surface  level pigment  some good ingredients for dealing with  pigment are retinoids hydroquinone  vitamin c butane kojic acid  niacinamide and licorice extract with  extracts be really careful because there  are lots of different types of extracts  and not all  licorice extracts will actually help  with pigment so make sure you look for a  product that actually specifies that  it's full pigment  if you have deeper pigment that these  skincare products aren't really helping  with  or if you're not sure how deep your  pigment is then go to a professional who  can diagnose your problem  and help you out with that so they can  put you on a treatment plan that  includes stronger treatments like  lasers and peels wrinkles come from  repeated movements as well as the  condition of your skin  you can think of it like a piece of  leather wrinkles will form when you fold  that leather repeatedly  this is why you might have heard of  preventative botox that actually stops  your face from moving  as much and so you don't get these  folded in wrinkles there are also  wrinkles called sleep wrinkles that come  from sleeping on your side or on your  front so your face basically gets  smushed up  and because we sleep for about a third  of our lives this smooshing can  etch in a wrinkle in our skin so for a  lot of people it can be worth it to  train yourself to sleep on your back  now some people shouldn't be doing this  because there might be other reasons  they're not sleeping on their back like  sleep apnea  now this is way more serious than sleep  wrinkles and for some people sleeping on  your back just decreases your quality of  sleep so much that it's not worth it it  can also have drawbacks  for people who want to try sleeping on  their back you don't have to have a  special pillow for this although it can  make it a bit more convenient  you can use wedge pillows or you can use  towels to try to keep your head  in one spot you can also try to use a  heavier quilt that sort of holds you in  place  now for makeup i'm still working on  trying to get my concealer to sit  properly  but angie from hot and flashy has tons  of great tips  using a primer underneath your concealer  can really help spread out the concealer  and keep it from shifting into those  lines  and this is a little bit  counter-intuitive but using less  concealer can actually help as well  because then there's less stuff that can  move with things like highlighters it's  good to avoid large particles because  they tend to settle into lines and make  them more obvious  so those are some of my tips for how to  change your routine as you get older  do you have any other tips let me know  in the comments if you liked the video  click the like and the subscribe you can  also follow me on instagram and check  out my blog for more nerdy science  content  thank you to foreign for sponsoring this  video and i will see you next time  you

